In response to the recent request for spoilers, here are some partial
answers:
(Spoilers coming up)

> Why can't I name my sword Excalibur?  What do I need to do?
Your long sword can become Excalibur if you dip it in a fountain,
and the Lady of the Lake reaches up and blesses it.  Excalibur is the
biggest name in weapons, as far as I know, so you can't just get one 
for nothing.  On the last version of hack whose code I looked at,
the name Excalibur made your sword do +rnd(10) damage every time it hit.
Also, at the time it becomes Excalibur the sword may actually be 
enchanted up to 5 points.  That is, a +5 long sword named Excalibur.
The other names (again, this info may be out of date) just add 1 to
the damage.  At least, Snickersnee does this for katanas, and Orcrist
does this for two-handed swords.  I don't know if Sting does anything.

Anyone else know?

